# Code owners for borromeanRings.
#
# GitHub requests review from an owner automatically when a matching path changes.
# This file NOMINATES reviewers; it does not REQUIRE them. Owner review only becomes
# mandatory once branch protection on `main` enables `require_code_owner_reviews`,
# which is currently false — see issue #60. Until then this is routing, not a gate.
#
# Later rules win, so the specific entries below override the catch-all.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule matches.
*                       @wimaan3

# The trust root. These decide whether anything else passes at all: the gate, the
# check registry, the policy spine, and the hooks that enforce governance in a session.
/verify.sh              @wimaan3
/merge.sh               @wimaan3
/checks/                @wimaan3
/src/meta_harness/      @wimaan3
/.claude/hooks/         @wimaan3
/borromeanrings.toml    @wimaan3

# Anything that reaches OUTSIDE this repository — into another project's config, or a
# user's global Claude settings. Two field bugs (#121, #125) have come from this seam.
/init.sh                @wimaan3
/adopt.sh               @wimaan3
/install-global.sh      @wimaan3

# Recorded decisions. An ADR is the durable record of why the code is shaped as it is.
/docs/adr/              @wimaan3
/docs/specs/            @wimaan3

# Supply chain and CI: what runs on GitHub's servers, and what gets installed.
/.github/workflows/     @wimaan3
/pyproject.toml         @wimaan3
/setup.cfg              @wimaan3
